# Varadaraj et al. (2026), "Euclid: Discovery of bright z~7 Lyman-break galaxies in UltraVISTA and Euclid COSMOS",
#   A&A 707, A239 (2026), doi:10.1051/0004-6361/202557508
# arXiv:2510.00945v2 (accepted version), Table 4 (tab:LF values), "UltraVISTA+Euclid" (U+E) columns
# Survey: UltraVISTA DR6 + Euclid COSMOS PV imaging (0.65 deg^2 for U+E); ground-based bright end
# Redshift: 6.5 <= z <= 7.5; representative z = 7.0
# x: M_UV from a 100 A top-hat at rest-frame 1500 A on the best-fit SED (= M1500); bins: 0.4 mag wide at
#    -22.6 and -22.2, 0.2 mag wide otherwise; phi is per mag
# Phi: linear, Mpc^-3 mag^-1 (written exactly as tabulated, in e-notation); symmetric 1-sigma error
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7
# The U+E sample is the one the paper fits (cleaner vs. brown dwarfs); its brightest bin (-22.6, 0 galaxies)
#   is a 1-sigma upper limit -> Varadaraj2026_ulimit/. n_gal (U+E): 3, 4, 6, 10, 19, 25, 27
